        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk: if July labor demand remains close to the Apr-May rebound and employers keep vacancies open despite soft payroll growth, the first print could land above the interval, especially above 7.84 million. Downside risk: if the May level was a temporary rebound and weak payroll hiring reflects broad demand cooling, July openings could fall back toward early-2026 levels and land below the interval. Outside the interval would require either a renewed vacancy surge above roughly 7.84 million or a sharp retracement below roughly 6.74 million."
